{"reference":"1 John 2","book":"1 John","chapter":2,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"chapter_overview","title":"Overview","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"The chapter moves from the reality of sin to a pattern of life shaped by knowing God. Jesus Christ is called the righteous Advocate with the Father, and he is described as hilasmos for sins, including those of the whole world. The writer then treats keeping God’s commandments and walking as Jesus walked as the test of knowing him. The commandment is both old and new: it is familiar from what the readers heard, yet its truth is shown in the movement from darkness to light and in love rather than hatred for a brother or sister.","verse_refs":["1 John 2:1","1 John 2:2","1 John 2:3-6","1 John 2:7-11"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_1_john_002_817a19c13ce07894d2c7d203","reader_path_1_john_002_cbb49f394b8311c20362b48e"],"confidence":"medium","interpretation_level":"disputed"},{"id":"block_2","text":"“World” in verses 15–17 cannot simply mean humanity, material creation, or culture, since the same term changes sense with context. Here the warning concerns the desires and boastful self-importance the passage associates with “the world,” which is passing away.","verse_refs":["1 John 2:15-17"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_1_john_002_af753fa36cbf0854b1089e4c","reader_path_1_john_002_c60747f81a0953ff24e0e643"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"},{"id":"block_3","text":"The “last hour” is presented as urgent, not as a timetable. The chapter speaks of many antichrists, connecting them with departure from the community and denial concerning Jesus, the Father, and the Son. Its plural language and polemical setting do not authorize speculative labeling of political or marginalized groups, and the opponents are known here only through the writer’s description.","verse_refs":["1 John 2:18","1 John 2:18-23"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_1_john_002_c60747f81a0953ff24e0e643","reader_path_1_john_002_cbb49f394b8311c20362b48e"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"},{"id":"block_4","text":"The repeated language of what remains or abides ties together the teaching heard from the beginning, life in the Son and Father, the anointing, and confidence at Christ’s manifestation. The anointing is said to teach and remain in the readers, but the passage itself is also written instruction; this language should not be treated as freedom from correction or as hostility to learning.","verse_refs":["1 John 2:20-27","1 John 2:24-28"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_1_john_002_ab99460763c80b50c11cc830","reader_path_1_john_002_cbb49f394b8311c20362b48e"],"confidence":"low","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]},{"kind":"language_literary","title":"Literary Connections","blocks":[{"id":"block_5","text":"The concentrated vocabulary, formulas, and concerns in this portion of 1 John are shared with 2 John, 3 John, and the Fourth Gospel. The literary relationship is clearer than any conclusion about which writing borrowed from another.","verse_refs":["1 John 2:7-27"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_1_john_002_fa3e46a7e1733068cd12e7db","reader_path_1_john_002_c60747f81a0953ff24e0e643"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]},{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"In the Wider Work","blocks":[{"id":"block_6","text":"The work does not name its writer, addressees, location, or destination. That absence means the chapter should not be read as if those details had been directly supplied.","verse_refs":["1 John 1:1-10","1 John 3:1-24","1 John 4:1-21","1 John 5:1-21"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_1_john_002_a0564f445b372cd4e3023529"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"fact"},{"id":"block_7","text":"The work’s language about sin should be read across its opening discussion of acknowledging sin and its later statements about sin. This wider context cautions against turning the opening of chapter 2 into a demand for sinless perfection or a source of shame.","verse_refs":["1 John 1:8-10"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_1_john_002_acea9edaa4cfd18466760d39"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}